#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f607558-5a7f-52df-b344-57f2f84791e9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cosine with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f6585d2-8d47-5fd8-8ead-623f2f938ecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341070} {:answer/id #uuid "a77bb6d5-3403-5cb2-be7a-22f9e89ebbcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341071} {:answer/id #uuid "38c504b4-1e59-5adb-bd98-489664ad1aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341072} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ff9b81-2481-5747-bc08-c47ead841607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341073} {:answer/id #uuid "44ea278d-01ad-5af8-9cc5-90e52de2e2c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f6585d2-8d47-5fd8-8ead-623f2f938ecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341070} :answer-field/id #uuid "d619dae3-71a5-54ca-96fa-4620bde81b8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c54e7d4-028f-5b21-afe7-a0c2c94b02e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-120896" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{7}{9}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{7}{9}) & =2.461\\,918…≈2.461\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2.461\\,9$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=2.461\\,9.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi -2.461\\,9 & ≈0.679\\,7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.679\\,7.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061537/assets/eafc9be7094c9c0ccdf167cc737d494efec40014a89ad793f7ed34ea5eed94ae.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.679\\,7 \\\\  & ≈3.821\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2.461\\,9\\cdot 3.821\\,3≈9\n$$\n\nto the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9f482ac-9771-52a3-9517-8494c3de6379" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cosine with Quadrantal Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f78f5cee-28b4-5244-91fa-cdb434b2f2c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f78f5cee-28b4-5244-91fa-cdb434b2f2c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341077} :answer-field/id #uuid "6589e7e6-be89-5fea-8d47-fdf742ef6b5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1671010-6b83-59b3-97e5-15e231262d67" :question/math-academy-id "q-274589" :question/problem "The solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-1$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-1$ correspond to the values of $x$ at which $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ attains its minimum value.\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-1)=\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\pi $ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is $x=\\pi .$\n\nThis solution is a quadrantal angle. To find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the cosine function. We know that the cosine function has its minimum values at\n\n$$\nx=\\pi +2n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSince the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x=\\pi $ is the only solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26666440-d376-5cb6-b922-9850e5c42eb3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cosine Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a24b3945-a887-57b0-ab23-12bb6c3cdfb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341080} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a8e648-cb33-5110-b2ae-ae9dcab518e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1a8e648-cb33-5110-b2ae-ae9dcab518e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341081} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a440afb-8163-5750-b01f-bfaee87ad826" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a81ae004-1067-5ca5-ae95-f9f2bf612e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a81ae004-1067-5ca5-ae95-f9f2bf612e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341083} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff8b6a73-8e21-5574-bcb8-694a83de4e7f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50552061-b7c2-53bb-b8b9-b421209c9dbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-338574" :question/problem "Arranged in **ascending order**, the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi $ are $x=${{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061537/assets/a22dba264faa711352724f135d2ec5a074202c4b5069dee2389fe954419a3770.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get a second solution that's within the required domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi $ from $X:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =X-2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}-2\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, arranged in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26666440-d376-5cb6-b922-9850e5c42eb3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cosine Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0492d6d-030f-5961-b2fc-3eda940bf6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0492d6d-030f-5961-b2fc-3eda940bf6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341086} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d1fa6f5-0a0e-59b4-b064-8f5a81099c18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341085} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26787f46-7591-5023-b5f9-5cb20f0b5e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26787f46-7591-5023-b5f9-5cb20f0b5e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341088} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a03e003-4760-5ad0-8561-c30ee6522015" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c06764c8-676c-57ec-8676-1a7cc0d09408" :question/math-academy-id "q-338710" :question/problem "Arranged in **ascending order** and rounded to **the nearest integer**, the solutions of the equation $4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2=-\\frac{1}{2}$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi $ are $x=${{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2 & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-\\frac{5}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{5}{8})=2.245\\,927…≈2.246\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2.246$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution, rounded to the nearest integer, is $x=2.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.896.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.896.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061537/assets/992325c7cbf34f4b981af0a9f34740990d39694e727861ca92bf591037436327.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.896 \\\\  & ≈4.038\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get a second solution that's within the required domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi $ from $X:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =X-2\\pi  \\\\  & =4.038-2\\pi  \\\\  & ≈-2.245 \\\\  & ≈-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, arranged in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2$ and $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f607558-5a7f-52df-b344-57f2f84791e9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cosine with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c74aa45-5cdb-5f18-9cc6-6f1589f15c86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341091} {:answer/id #uuid "97dca764-ca3b-5349-bdda-0d982c02f676" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341092} {:answer/id #uuid "c1cabf25-c77d-5b8a-94e2-4945e940b858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341093} {:answer/id #uuid "36b42eb4-3947-5988-bc74-a6047d54f3e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341094} {:answer/id #uuid "3776c6fd-cb2e-5507-b0ac-402805428f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97dca764-ca3b-5349-bdda-0d982c02f676" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341092} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2f7243d-24c5-5331-8385-79d54c554964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8530205e-bf53-5ec7-b72c-631c4c27fbb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-72835" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{2}{3}) & =2.300\\,523…≈2.301\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2.301$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=2.301.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi -2.301 & ≈0.841.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.841.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061537/assets/d02a0250df0f0e6c389594ea0e1b119d9f4c63c353553d56c0e865f487862284.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.841 \\\\  & ≈3.983\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}≈2.301\\cdot 3.983≈9\n$$\n\nto the nearest integer."}]}
